    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0366" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg326"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1359.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 21, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of 30th ultimo, No. 910,
                    relative to the state of opinion in England, and your suggestions as to the
                    expediency of pressing upon the British government the necessity of withdrawing
                    from the rebels their recognition of them as belligerents, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., London.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
